.TH ZEX-ROLLBACK 1 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-rollback \- revert a package transaction
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elevate zex rollback
.RI [ \-\-list ]
.RI [ <tx-id> ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex rollback
restores the system to the state captured at a previous transaction snapshot.
.PP
Every install, upgrade, and remove operation writes a snapshot to
.IR /overlayer/zexlib/transactions/ .
.B zex rollback
reads the snapshot and reverses the recorded changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
List available transaction snapshots with their timestamps and operations.
.TP
.I <tx-id>
The transaction ID to roll back to (from
.B \-\-list
output).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Rollback successful.
.TP
.B 1
Transaction not found, snapshot corrupt, or insufficient privileges.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex rollback --list
    elevate zex rollback tx-1719446400000
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-install (1),
.BR zex-update (1)
